In any case, I'll administer an anesthetic and you won't feel a thing.

132
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:12,640
Alright, so the topic of today's lesson is toothache but it's also basically about learning that you will have to have your tooth taken out.

133
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,720
So to say this we say, to pull out a tooth.

134
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,080
Okay, so that's what the dentist said.

135
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:20,560
I think we may have to pull out your wisdom tooth.

136
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,920
Not good news.

137
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:24,460
Okay, so to pull out means to extract.

138
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:28,360
So just remember here this is a phrase that has pull out.

139
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,160
Out would be the preposition here.

140
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:33,240
We wouldn't say pull off or pull at.

141
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,240
We'd say pull out.

142
00:07:34,510 --> 00:07:37,010
Like for example, you can pull out a hair or your hair.

143
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:37,530
Exactly.

144
00:07:37,890 --> 00:07:46,310
Okay, so we're pulling out the wisdom tooth and the dentist first wants to take some x-rays to see what we're dealing with.

145
00:07:46,790 --> 00:07:53,330
Okay, so to deal with something means to work on it or to have something to do with.

146
00:07:53,830 --> 00:07:56,210
And so in this case the dentist wants to know, is this serious?

147
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,960
What are we dealing with here?

148
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,960
That's right.

149
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:01,170
So he's trying to judge the situation.

150
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:08,020
So maybe what would be another scenario or another situation where you would say, I have to see what we're dealing with.

151
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:19,600
Well, in the case of the weather and the newsmen who report about the weather, maybe they see that a storm is coming but they have to look at the radars and the computer screens to see what they're dealing with.

152
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:23,340
Is it a serious storm or is it a very weak storm?

153
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:24,680
They have to evaluate.

154
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:25,680
That's right.

155
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:26,920
Okay, very good.

156
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,680
And so we're going to see what we're dealing with.

157
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:33,880
And then the girl I think knows that she hasn't really taken good care of her teeth.

158
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:38,800
And so she says, I guess that's what I get for not flossing or brushing my teeth.

159
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:41,520
So that's what you get or that's what I get.

160
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:49,000
Where the pronoun changes, I, you, he, that's what I get for not taking care of myself.

161
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,980
This means it's my fault.

162
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,020
I deserved it.

163
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,280
I deserve this thing.

164
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:56,620
So I could say, Marco, that's what you get for not doing your homework.

165
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,460
You got a bad grade on your test.

166
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,120
That's right.

167
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:02,310
So it's basically a way of saying, that's what you deserve.

168
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:04,270
That's the consequence for your actions.

169
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,080
Exactly.

170
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,080
Okay.

171
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,080
And what about our last phrase?

172
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:12,250
This is something that I hate to hear from doctors and dentists because usually it's a lie.

173
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:18,590
A dentist will say before he gives you a shot or before he takes your tooth out, you won't feel a thing.

174
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:19,450
That's right.

175
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:23,190
So he's basically saying you're not going to feel any pain.

176
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:27,720
But why do we say you won't feel a thing instead of you won't feel anything?

177
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:29,760
Just a set phrase.

178
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:34,160
It's something we say, I would remember it like this because it's more likely to be said in this way.

179
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,660
You won't feel a thing.

180
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:40,280
I think it basically means not even one little thing, you're not going to feel that.

181
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:47,460
So for example, I'm about to fix someone's back, you know, when you have to pull them and make their back feel better.

182
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:49,100
I say, you won't feel a thing.

183
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,400
You fix their back.

184
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,400
Okay.

185
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,600
So you won't feel a thing or you won't feel anything.

186
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:59,360
Both are correct, but I think it's more common to hear you won't feel a thing.

187
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:00,340
Okay.

188
